*  PAD_driver - exercises PAD(S,CW): add or delete blanks in S to make it
*  conform to a column width of CW.  Contract per PAD.sno header.  Brackets
*  make the added and deleted blanks visible.  Cases: a string shorter than
*  the width (blanks added), one longer (blanks deleted), one already at the
*  width, a string with no interior blanks to work with, and a single word.
-INCLUDE "PAD.sno"
        OUTPUT  =  '[' PAD('a b c', 11) ']'
        OUTPUT  =  '[' PAD('one two three four', 12) ']'
        OUTPUT  =  '[' PAD('a b c', 5) ']'
        OUTPUT  =  '[' PAD('abcdef', 10) ']'
        OUTPUT  =  '[' PAD('word', 8) ']'
        OUTPUT  =  '[' PAD('the  quick   brown fox', 20) ']'
END
